00:33:11,675 --> 00:33:16,425
That lecherous, ogling, cunning Prince Asdollah-Mirza,

852
00:33:16,550 --> 00:33:17,800
He sent him to your house…

853
00:33:17,800 --> 00:33:19,800
To spend the night with your wife, Aziz-Saltaneh,

854
00:33:19,800 --> 00:33:20,800
So she wouldn't be scared!

855
00:33:20,800 --> 00:33:22,175
Him!!! Don’t shout-

856
00:33:22,300 --> 00:33:23,300
Of course, Lady Aziz

857
00:33:23,300 --> 00:33:25,091
Isn't someone such rumors would stick to!

858
00:33:25,341 --> 00:33:26,841
But what about the neighbors' gossip?

859
00:33:27,300 --> 00:33:29,300
The Prince went to my house tonight?

860
00:33:29,300 --> 00:33:29,716
Shh!

861
00:33:29,800 --> 00:33:31,300
To be with my wife?

862
00:33:31,300 --> 00:33:32,091
Don’t shout!

863
00:33:32,091 --> 00:33:35,091
That lecherous good-for-nothing idiot

864
00:33:35,175 --> 00:33:36,091
Went to my house?

865
00:33:36,175 --> 00:33:36,550
Don’t shout!

866
00:33:36,591 --> 00:33:38,216
With my wife? Don’t make a fuss, Dustali!-

867
00:33:38,300 --> 00:33:39,800
I'll make his mother mourn him! Dustali!-

868
00:33:39,800 --> 00:33:40,675
Don’t get upset!

869
00:33:40,716 --> 00:33:42,050
Don't make a fuss over nothing, Dustali!

870
00:33:42,300 --> 00:33:43,966
Asdollah-Mirza isn't the kind of man who…

871
00:33:43,966 --> 00:33:45,425
Asdollah isn't the kind of man who what?

872
00:33:45,425 --> 00:33:46,050
Don’t get upset!

873
00:33:46,050 --> 00:33:47,675
You don’t know that rotten scoundrel!

874
00:33:47,675 --> 00:33:49,050
I myself am afraid

875
00:33:49,050 --> 00:33:51,175
To be alone with that home-wrecker! Shh! Shh!-

876
00:33:51,216 --> 00:33:53,050
I'll make this Prince pay dearly!

877
00:33:53,091 --> 00:33:53,675
All right, that's enough!

878
00:33:53,716 --> 00:33:55,800
I'll get rid of this home-wrecker!

879
00:33:55,841 --> 00:33:56,175
Shh!-

880
00:33:56,175 --> 00:33:57,091
He goes to my house?

881
00:33:57,175 --> 00:33:58,216
I know what to do with him!

882
00:33:58,216 --> 00:33:58,716
Shout!

883
00:33:58,716 --> 00:33:59,550
I'll make him pay!

884
00:33:59,550 --> 00:34:01,050
I'll ruin him!

885
00:34:03,925 --> 00:34:04,466
Ahh…

886
00:34:08,925 --> 00:34:13,550
Mahur Piece – Faramarz Payvar and Hossein Tehrani

887
00:34:28,675 --> 00:34:29,716
Lady Aziz!

888
00:34:35,175 --> 00:34:36,216
Who is it?

889
00:34:39,925 --> 00:34:40,466
Who is it?

890
00:34:40,925 --> 00:34:41,550
Lady Aziz!

891
00:34:41,675 --> 00:34:42,466
What's going on!

892
00:34:42,550 --> 00:34:43,050
It's me!

893
00:34:43,425 --> 00:34:43,841
Open!

894
00:34:46,425 --> 00:34:48,175
Open the door quickly, Lady Aziz!

895
00:34:48,466 --> 00:34:49,966
Open up, let me in!

896
00:34:50,050 --> 00:34:52,050
For God's sake, open this door and let me in!

897
00:34:52,716 --> 00:34:53,800
What do you want, Saeid?

898
00:34:53,925 --> 00:34:54,466
What is it?

899
00:34:54,550 --> 00:34:55,050
What's going on?

900
00:34:55,966 --> 00:34:56,800
Uncle Asdollah!

901
00:34:58,091 --> 00:34:58,716
Uncle Asdollah!

902
00:34:59,550 --> 00:35:00,300
Uncle Asdollah!

903
00:35:00,300 --> 00:35:01,175
What's going on, Saeid! Wh… what's wrong with you!

904
00:35:01,216 --> 00:35:01,925
Uncle Asdollah, run!

905
00:35:01,925 --> 00:35:02,175
Huh!

906
00:35:02,175 --> 00:35:03,216
Quick, run! Tell me what's going on!-

907
00:35:03,216 --> 00:35:03,966
What's going on?

908
00:35:04,050 --> 00:35:04,841
Run, run!

909
00:35:04,925 --> 00:35:06,216
Agha Joon found Dustali-Khan

910
00:35:06,216 --> 00:35:08,300
And told him you spent tonight with Lady Aziz!

911
00:35:08,300 --> 00:35:09,300
Oh, no…!

912
00:35:09,300 --> 00:35:10,800
Now who's going to deal with this jackass!

913
00:35:10,800 --> 00:35:11,841
Leave him to me, Asdollah!

914
00:35:11,841 --> 00:35:13,300
What's wrong? Why are you afraid? Lady Aziz, let him run!-

915
00:35:13,341 --> 00:35:15,425
Dustali-Khan's eyes were bloodshot with rage!

916
00:35:15,466 --> 00:35:16,216
Don’t be afraid, dear!

917
00:35:16,300 --> 00:35:18,300
♪ Tombak percussion ♪

918
00:35:24,966 --> 00:35:26,216
(Knocking on door)

919
00:35:26,300 --> 00:35:28,050
Dustali can't do a damn thing!

920
00:35:28,050 --> 00:35:29,550
This guy, where's the Aspiran? Open! (He pounds on the door)-

921
00:35:29,591 --> 00:35:31,091
Tell him to go stop him, quick! Open the door!-

922
00:35:31,175 --> 00:35:32,675
He went out to buy wine!

923
00:35:32,675 --> 00:35:33,341
Open!

924
00:35:34,425 --> 00:35:35,716
If you're a man, come open the door!

925
00:35:35,716 --> 00:35:36,841
You lecherous creep!

926
00:35:36,925 --> 00:35:38,675
If you've got the guts, come open the door!

927
00:35:38,716 --> 00:35:39,925
Oh, no, no!

928
00:35:40,216 --> 00:35:42,425
He… he… he's going to break the door down!

929
00:35:42,800 --> 00:35:45,300
Woman, show me somewhere to hide!

930
00:35:45,341 --> 00:35:45,841
Under the bed! Open the door!-

931
00:35:45,925 --> 00:35:46,341
No!

932
00:35:46,966 --> 00:35:47,716
In the trunk!

933
00:35:47,716 --> 00:35:48,425
I'll suffocate!

934
00:35:49,091 --> 00:35:49,800
In the closet!

935
00:35:49,800 --> 00:35:51,591
No! Husbands always check the closet first!

936
00:35:51,675 --> 00:35:52,550
Open the door!

937
00:35:56,425 --> 00:35:57,550
Open the door!

938
00:35:57,550 --> 00:35:59,300
You creep! When I get in,

939
00:35:59,300 --> 00:36:00,216
I'll make your mother mourn you! The roof!-

940
00:36:00,300 --> 00:36:02,175
Escape over the roof! Yes! The stairs are there! Run!-

941
00:36:02,216 --> 00:36:03,425
I owe you one

942
00:36:03,425 --> 00:36:04,925
For saving me from this wild bear!

943
00:36:05,300 --> 00:36:07,091
Open this damn door!

944
00:36:08,675 --> 00:36:09,925
If you're a man, come out!

945
00:36:09,925 --> 00:36:10,425
Who is it?

946
00:36:10,425 --> 00:36:11,341
If you're a man, open this door! Coming!-

947
00:36:11,800 --> 00:36:12,966
What is it? What's going on!

948
00:36:13,425 --> 00:36:14,425
Where is this lowlife?

949
00:36:14,675 --> 00:36:16,550
Where have you even been all this time? Where is this home-wrecker?-

950
00:36:16,550 --> 00:36:18,341
And he's the one complaining! Where is he! Where is he!-

951
00:36:20,550 --> 00:36:21,800
What are you looking for?

952
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:22,841
For that home-wrecker!

953
00:36:22,841 --> 00:36:24,091
For that lecherous creep!

954
00:36:24,300 --> 00:36:24,925
Where is he?

955
00:36:25,216 --> 00:36:27,550
Where is this shameless Prince Asdollah!

956
00:36:27,550 --> 00:36:28,466
Where is he!

957
00:36:31,175 --> 00:36:32,050
I'll find him!

958
00:36:32,050 --> 00:36:32,800
Have you gone mad!

959
00:36:32,841 --> 00:36:33,800
I said, who are you looking for?

960
00:36:33,800 --> 00:36:34,175
Where is he?

961
00:36:34,216 --> 00:36:35,675
Where did you hide him?

962
00:36:36,300 --> 00:36:37,675
I didn't hide anyone!

963
00:36:37,925 --> 00:36:39,091
I'll deal with you soon!

964
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:41,675
Why on earth would Asdollah be here?

965
00:36:41,675 --> 00:36:42,425
Shame on you!

966
00:36:42,425 --> 00:36:43,425
You've gone too far!

967
00:36:43,925 --> 00:36:45,300
Tell me where you hid him!

968
00:36:45,675 --> 00:36:47,591
I'll make his mother mourn him!

969
00:36:47,800 --> 00:36:50,050
I swear by God, by the saints, by the Prophet, (Someone knocks)

970
00:36:50,050 --> 00:36:50,675
He's not here!

971
00:36:50,675 --> 00:36:52,050
I swear on Great Sir's soul!

972
00:36:52,050 --> 00:36:53,175
(Someone knocks)

973
00:36:54,716 --> 00:36:55,425
I'll find him!

974
00:36:59,300 --> 00:37:00,050
Stop!

975
00:37:00,341 --> 00:37:01,216
Stay right there!

976
00:37:01,591 --> 00:37:02,550
Don't move!

977
00:37:03,425 --> 00:37:03,800
Stop!

978
00:37:04,800 --> 00:37:05,300
Stop!

979
00:37:06,341 --> 00:37:06,925
Stop!

980
00:37:08,175 --> 00:37:08,925
Stop!

981
00:37:12,591 --> 00:37:15,800
Lady, I couldn't find the wine you wanted.

982
00:37:15,966 --> 00:37:18,050
I bought you a different wine.

983
00:37:20,925 --> 00:37:21,675
Huh!

984
00:37:22,050 --> 00:37:24,175
You're not Lady Aziz!

985
00:37:24,800 --> 00:37:25,300
Where is she?

986
00:37:25,300 --> 00:37:26,091
Where did she go?

987
00:37:26,425 --> 00:37:28,550
Quick, fast, swift, immediately: answer!

988
00:37:46,216 --> 00:37:46,966
Uncle Asdollah!

989
00:37:48,675 --> 00:37:50,175
Uncle Asdollah, it's broken here!

990
00:37:50,966 --> 00:37:52,050
Then go search over there.

991
00:37:52,050 --> 00:37:53,550
We have to find a way!

992
00:37:53,591 --> 00:37:55,175
Before the roof collapses under us! Go!-

993
00:37:55,800 --> 00:37:57,550
Hurry, find a way!

994
00:37:57,550 --> 00:37:58,716
But it's dark!

995
00:37:58,716 --> 00:38:00,175
Search over there! Search over there!

996
00:38:02,800 --> 00:38:04,216
If there's a way, come tell me!

997
00:38:04,341 --> 00:38:04,800
Come quickly.

998
00:38:04,841 --> 00:38:05,925
You lowlife! Ow ow ow…-

999
00:38:05,966 --> 00:38:08,175
You came to steal again?

1000
00:38:08,466 --> 00:38:09,300
Uncle Asdollah! Oh no!-

1001
00:38:09,466 --> 00:38:09,966
My neck!

1002
00:38:10,050 --> 00:38:12,675
Lowlife! We've lain in wait for you for nights!

1003
00:38:12,675 --> 00:38:13,216
My neck!

1004
00:38:13,216 --> 00:38:14,841
Now we've got you! Ow ow…-

1005
00:38:14,925 --> 00:38:15,716
My neck!

1006
00:38:16,300 --> 00:38:17,050
Oh, my neck!

1007
00:38:17,050 --> 00:38:17,675
My neck!

1008
00:38:18,050 --> 00:38:19,341
Huh! Is that you, Shir-Ali?

1009
00:38:19,550 --> 00:38:20,591
Let go of my neck!

1010
00:38:20,591 --> 00:38:21,925
Sir, we didn't recognize you!

1011
00:38:21,925 --> 00:38:23,300
We mistook you for a thief.

1012
00:38:23,300 --> 00:38:24,591
Sir, what are you doing

1013
00:38:24,675 --> 00:38:25,800
On the roof? Don’t ask, Shir-Ali!-

1014
00:38:25,800 --> 00:38:26,800
Don’t ask!

1015
00:38:26,841 --> 00:38:29,050
Because people are so wicked! So evil!

1016
00:38:29,175 --> 00:38:30,550
We're at your service!

1017
00:38:30,591 --> 00:38:31,800
If anyone wishes you harm,

1018
00:38:31,800 --> 00:38:33,466
Just call from behind the wall,

1019
00:38:33,550 --> 00:38:35,341
"Shir-Ali, get up and come!"

1020
00:38:35,675 --> 00:38:37,466
Then leave the rest to me!

1021
00:38:37,550 --> 00:38:38,091
This Dustali!

1022
00:38:38,300 --> 00:38:39,925
Over that property dispute,

1023
00:38:39,966 --> 00:38:41,050
Remember, a few years ago?

1024
00:38:41,050 --> 00:38:41,550
Yes, Sir!

1025
00:38:41,800 --> 00:38:43,675
He invited me to his house.

1026
00:38:43,925 --> 00:38:45,841
Little did I know he wanted revenge!

1027
00:38:46,050 --> 00:38:47,050
So I went to his house!

1028
00:38:47,091 --> 00:38:48,550
The scoundrel himself wasn't there!

1029
00:38:49,216 --> 00:38:50,675
I sat chatting with his wife,

1030
00:38:50,675 --> 00:38:52,300
When suddenly he burst in unannounced

1031
00:38:52,341 --> 00:38:53,800
And accused me of dishonorable things!

1032
00:38:53,841 --> 00:38:54,925
Have you ever seen anyone

1033
00:38:54,925 --> 00:38:56,466
Who, just to torment people,

1034
00:38:56,466 --> 00:38:59,050
Is willing to slander his own wife's honor?

1035
00:38:59,216 --> 00:39:00,425
Is that true, Sir?

1036
00:39:00,425 --> 00:39:02,050
To hell with his honor!

1037
00:39:02,050 --> 00:39:04,300
If he had any honor, he wouldn't slander people!

1038
00:39:06,550 --> 00:39:07,550
Tahereh!

1039
00:39:11,425 --> 00:39:12,675
Tahereh!

1040
00:39:15,675 --> 00:39:16,300
What is it?

1041
00:39:16,550 --> 00:39:17,675
What is it, Shir-Ali?

1042
00:39:18,050 --> 00:39:18,800
Tahereh!

1043
00:39:19,050 --> 00:39:20,800
Bring that cleaver up here!

1044
00:39:22,925 --> 00:39:23,591
Cleaver?

1045
00:39:24,175 --> 00:39:25,550
What are you going to do, Shir-Ali?

1046
00:39:26,925 --> 00:39:28,466
Just say the word, Sir!

1047
00:39:28,550 --> 00:39:30,216
And I'll spill his guts!

1048
00:39:30,216 --> 00:39:30,925
Moment!

1049
00:39:31,050 --> 00:39:31,800
Moment!

1050
00:39:31,800 --> 00:39:33,050
Please, Shir-Ali!

1051
00:39:33,050 --> 00:39:34,050
There'll be a scandal!

1052
00:39:34,050 --> 00:39:35,675
I'll hide somewhere tonight

1053
00:39:35,675 --> 00:39:36,425
Until tomorrow!

1054
00:39:36,425 --> 00:39:38,550
For now, let this disgraceful man calm down!

1055
00:39:38,675 --> 00:39:41,300
Stay at our house tonight.

1056
00:39:41,425 --> 00:39:43,300
You're most welcome!

1057
00:39:43,550 --> 00:39:45,300
I'll make up a bed for you in the basement,

1058
00:39:45,300 --> 00:39:46,466
Come and sleep.

1059
00:39:46,550 --> 00:39:48,300
Bless you, Shir-Ali!

1060
00:39:48,716 --> 00:39:50,050
You're a brother to us!

1061
00:39:52,091 --> 00:39:53,841
You'd better go ahead first

1062
00:39:53,841 --> 00:39:55,175
And let your wife know.

1063
00:39:55,425 --> 00:39:56,966
I shouldn't come to your house unannounced!

1064
00:39:56,966 --> 00:39:58,591
God forbid!

1065
00:39:58,675 --> 00:40:00,425
Mr. Asdollah-Mirza!

1066
00:40:00,675 --> 00:40:02,841
Such talk doesn't suit you.

1067
00:40:03,091 --> 00:40:06,175
Anyway, Sir, a woman has to be decent herself!

1068
00:40:06,175 --> 00:40:06,550
Yes, that's right.

1069
00:40:06,925 --> 00:40:07,800
Mr. Asdollah-Mirza,

1070
00:40:07,925 --> 00:40:10,050
You're like a brother to me.

1071
00:40:10,466 --> 00:40:12,091
This wife of mine

1072
00:40:12,300 --> 00:40:13,800
Could be Lady Aziz's granddaughter!

1073
00:40:13,800 --> 00:40:15,341
Not at all! Not at all!

1074
00:40:15,341 --> 00:40:15,675
You'd

1075
00:40:15,716 --> 00:40:16,675
Compare Lady Tahereh

1076
00:40:16,675 --> 00:40:17,591
With that she-devil?

1077
00:40:17,675 --> 00:40:18,800
Really!

1078
00:40:18,841 --> 00:40:20,550
A young wife, Sir…

1079
00:40:20,591 --> 00:40:22,175
After all…

1080
00:40:22,216 --> 00:40:24,300
Men are always circling around her.

1081
00:40:24,800 --> 00:40:26,300
But my wife…

1082
00:40:26,841 --> 00:40:28,466
First of all…

1083
00:40:28,550 --> 00:40:30,425
She never leaves the house.

1084
00:40:30,800 --> 00:40:31,841
Second of all…

1085
00:40:31,841 --> 00:40:33,425
Well… now you go ahead…

1086
00:40:33,425 --> 00:40:34,175
Let her know!

1087
00:40:34,591 --> 00:40:36,175
Yes, Sir!

1088
00:40:36,716 --> 00:40:38,925
But excuse me for going first!

1089
00:40:41,091 --> 00:40:42,050
Bless you.

1090
00:40:42,425 --> 00:40:43,175
Saeid!

1091
00:40:43,591 --> 00:40:44,550
What is it, uncle?

1092
00:40:47,300 --> 00:40:47,800
My boy!

1093
00:40:47,966 --> 00:40:48,716
You go home.

1094
00:40:48,966 --> 00:40:50,716
And you don't know where I am!

1095
00:40:50,800 --> 00:40:51,300
Understood?

1096
00:40:55,966 --> 00:40:56,841
Tahereh!

1097
00:40:57,550 --> 00:40:58,425
Eh! What is it?

1098
00:40:58,466 --> 00:40:59,675
We have a guest tonight.

1099
00:40:59,675 --> 00:41:01,466
Is there anything you need me to bring?

1100
00:41:01,550 --> 00:41:02,800
No, dear, everything's here!

1101
00:41:02,800 --> 00:41:04,175
Just remember,

1102
00:41:04,175 --> 00:41:05,425
You don't know where I am!

1103
00:41:05,550 --> 00:41:06,841
Especially to that she-devil,

1104
00:41:06,925 --> 00:41:07,675
Aziz-Saltaneh,

1105
00:41:07,716 --> 00:41:08,675
Don't say a word!

1106
00:41:08,675 --> 00:41:09,925
Don't worry!

1107
00:41:09,925 --> 00:41:10,425
OK!

1108
00:41:10,925 --> 00:41:12,300
Goodbye, Uncle Asdollah.

1109
00:41:12,800 --> 00:41:13,675
May you live long, young man!

1110
00:41:13,675 --> 00:41:16,175
Remember, if you're ever in trouble,

1111
00:41:16,175 --> 00:41:16,675
Tell your uncle!

1112
00:41:16,716 --> 00:41:17,175
Okay…

1113
00:41:17,550 --> 00:41:18,050
Oh, lovely!

1114
00:41:22,050 --> 00:41:23,300
Hurry up, Tahereh!

1115
00:41:23,300 --> 00:41:25,675
I said make up a bed for Sir in the basement!

1116
00:41:27,091 --> 00:41:28,425
Come in, Sir.

1117
00:41:28,466 --> 00:41:29,925
Make yourself at home.

1118
00:41:30,800 --> 00:41:32,175
You're most welcome.

1119
00:41:32,425 --> 00:41:33,425
Come in.

1120
00:41:34,133 --> 00:41:38,758
Mahur Piece – Faramarz Payvar and Hossein Tehrani

1121
00:41:51,300 --> 00:41:52,425
He'll end up

1122
00:41:52,466 --> 00:41:53,966
Killing me!

1123
00:41:53,966 --> 00:41:55,091
Dustali-Khan would have to

1124
00:41:55,091 --> 00:41:57,966
Walk over our dead bodies to kill you!

1125
00:41:58,091 --> 00:42:00,091
Anyone who even looks crooked at the door of this house,

1126
00:42:00,175 --> 00:42:02,550
Your servant will split him in two!

1127
00:42:03,341 --> 00:42:05,300
So far, we've split two men in half…

1128
00:42:05,550 --> 00:42:06,675
And properly too!

1129
00:42:07,341 --> 00:42:09,341
♪ Birds singing ♪

1130
00:42:25,800 --> 00:42:26,425
Saeid!

1131
00:42:27,175 --> 00:42:27,716
Saeid, dear?

1132
00:42:29,341 --> 00:42:30,091
Come here.

1133
00:42:33,300 --> 00:42:34,050
Hello, Lady Aziz.

1134
00:42:34,175 --> 00:42:34,800
Hello!

1135
00:42:36,300 --> 00:42:37,675
How lucky I ran into you!

1136
00:42:37,925 --> 00:42:38,300
Saeid!

1137
00:42:38,300 --> 00:42:39,300
Tell me the truth!

1138
00:42:39,341 --> 00:42:41,175
Don't you know where Asdollah went last night?

1139
00:42:41,425 --> 00:42:42,341
Honestly, Lady Aziz…

1140
00:42:42,466 --> 00:42:44,300
Last night, when Dustali-Khan showed up,

1141
00:42:44,341 --> 00:42:45,341
I was so scared

1142
00:42:45,425 --> 00:42:46,550
I wasn't paying attention to anything!

1143
00:42:46,550 --> 00:42:47,216
First…

1144
00:42:47,300 --> 00:42:49,425
We went over the roofs to near the ditch!

1145
00:42:49,425 --> 00:42:49,675
Well?

1146
00:42:49,925 --> 00:42:51,925
We jumped off a wall into the alley!

1147
00:42:52,175 --> 00:42:52,716
Then Uncle Asdollah

1148
00:42:52,800 --> 00:42:54,550
Sent me home and went off himself!

1149
00:42:55,050 --> 00:42:56,175
He jumped off a wall?

1150
00:42:56,175 --> 00:42:56,800
Yes!

1151
00:42:57,216 --> 00:42:58,800
Oh, you rascal, Asdollah!

1152
00:42:58,800 --> 00:43:00,050
The things you do!

1153
00:43:00,591 --> 00:43:02,300
Tell me, didn't you see where he went?

1154
00:43:02,550 --> 00:43:03,341
Honestly, I don't know!

1155
00:43:03,425 --> 00:43:04,425
Maybe he went home.

1156
00:43:04,425 --> 00:43:05,050
Home?

1157
00:43:05,091 --> 00:43:07,050
No, he didn't go home last night!

1158
00:43:07,550 --> 00:43:08,716
I'm very worried about him.

1159
00:43:08,966 --> 00:43:10,175
This idiot Dustali

1160
00:43:10,175 --> 00:43:11,966
Has gotten some fantasies into his head!

1161
00:43:12,050 --> 00:43:13,466
He's sworn to kill Asdollah!

1162
00:43:13,800 --> 00:43:14,425
Kill?

1163
00:43:14,675 --> 00:43:15,966
How dare he!

1164
00:43:15,966 --> 00:43:16,925
Over my dead body!

1165
00:43:17,675 --> 00:43:18,550
Dustali…

1166
00:43:18,550 --> 00:43:20,300
Doesn't have the guts for such things!

1167
00:43:20,341 --> 00:43:21,925
But you never know, he might snap!

1168
00:43:22,550 --> 00:43:23,175
Look…

1169
00:43:23,216 --> 00:43:24,050
Saeid dear!

1170
00:43:24,966 --> 00:43:27,175
If Dustali ever asks you anything,

1171
00:43:27,175 --> 00:43:28,466
Don't say a word!

1172
00:43:28,800 --> 00:43:30,841
No! Don't worry, Lady Aziz.

1173
00:43:30,966 --> 00:43:32,425
I didn't see anything at all!

1174
00:43:32,425 --> 00:43:34,050
By the way, that Nayeb inspector!

1175
00:43:34,091 --> 00:43:35,300
The Aspiran! What did you do with him?

1176
00:43:35,341 --> 00:43:35,925
Nothing!

1177
00:43:35,925 --> 00:43:37,550
I put him in the alley and shut the door!

1178
00:43:37,800 --> 00:43:39,175
Now that Dustali has turned up,

1179
00:43:39,175 --> 00:43:40,425
That jackass has no business

1180
00:43:40,425 --> 00:43:41,300
Staying at our house!

1181
00:43:42,050 --> 00:43:43,341
Oh… listen…

1182
00:43:43,675 --> 00:43:45,216
I'm going to drop in on your aunt.

1183
00:43:45,300 --> 00:43:46,716
Then I'll go to Asdollah's house.

1184
00:43:47,550 --> 00:43:49,050
If he turns up,

1185
00:43:49,050 --> 00:43:51,050
Tell him to stay out of sight today.

1186
00:43:51,341 --> 00:43:52,716
Tell him not to go to the office either!

1187
00:43:53,300 --> 00:43:56,216
This idiot Dustali might make a scene!

1188
00:43:56,300 --> 00:43:56,716
Okay!

1189
00:43:57,800 --> 00:43:59,091
Don't forget, huh!

1190
00:43:59,175 --> 00:44:00,550
If Dustali ever

1191
00:44:00,550 --> 00:44:01,425
Asks you anything,

1192
00:44:01,425 --> 00:44:02,091
Don't say a word!

1193
00:44:02,091 --> 00:44:03,425
Good boy! Don't worry!-

1194
00:44:27,216 --> 00:44:28,466
What are you sewing, Mash Ghasem?

1195
00:44:29,550 --> 00:44:30,550
Pants!

1196
00:44:31,591 --> 00:44:34,550
We've run around after everyone so much lately

1197
00:44:34,591 --> 00:44:36,550
That we tore the seat of our pants!

1198
00:44:39,800 --> 00:44:41,175
By the way, my boy!

1199
00:44:41,300 --> 00:44:42,466
Wasn't that Lady Aziz

1200
00:44:42,550 --> 00:44:45,050
Talking to you in the yard?

1201
00:44:45,466 --> 00:44:46,091
Yes!

1202
00:44:46,800 --> 00:44:48,800
She came asking about Uncle Asdollah.

1203
00:44:49,675 --> 00:44:51,466
Do you know where Uncle Asdollah is?

1204
00:44:51,841 --> 00:44:53,341
At dawn this morning,

1205
00:44:53,466 --> 00:44:55,591
Sir sent us after him.

1206
00:44:56,050 --> 00:44:57,800
He hadn't gone home at all last night!

1207
00:44:59,466 --> 00:45:01,175
And Mr. Shamsali-Mirza,

1208
00:45:01,175 --> 00:45:03,675
We told him what went on here last night!

1209
00:45:03,716 --> 00:45:05,050
He got very worried!

1210
00:45:05,300 --> 00:45:05,841
Last night?

1211
00:45:06,675 --> 00:45:07,175
Here?

1212
00:45:07,675 --> 00:45:08,800
What went on, Mash Ghasem?

1213
00:45:10,675 --> 00:45:12,716
Last night, with all the racket here,

1214
00:45:12,800 --> 00:45:14,175
Where were you?

1215
00:45:14,175 --> 00:45:14,591
I…

1216
00:45:14,675 --> 00:45:16,300
Honestly, I don't know! Maybe I was asleep!

1217
00:45:17,550 --> 00:45:19,050
God spare you!

1218
00:45:20,550 --> 00:45:21,425
Last night…

1219
00:45:21,425 --> 00:45:23,175
Mr. Dustali-Khan came

1220
00:45:23,175 --> 00:45:23,925
Gun in hand,

1221
00:45:23,925 --> 00:45:24,591
To see Sir!

1222
00:45:25,175 --> 00:45:27,341
Sir told him Mr. Asdollah-Khan wasn't there!

1223
00:45:27,675 --> 00:45:28,716
He didn't believe it!

1224
00:45:29,800 --> 00:45:32,675
He went and searched all the rooms!

1225
00:45:33,841 --> 00:45:35,716
Sir got angry too,

1226
00:45:35,716 --> 00:45:36,800
He was furious,

1227
00:45:36,800 --> 00:45:37,550
Two slaps,

1228
00:45:37,591 --> 00:45:38,425
Smack! Smack!

1229
00:45:38,425 --> 00:45:39,716
Right across his face!

1230
00:45:40,925 --> 00:45:42,300
Mr. Dustali-Khan

1231
00:45:42,300 --> 00:45:43,341
Had sworn

1232
00:45:43,425 --> 00:45:45,425
To empty his gun

1233
00:45:45,425 --> 00:45:48,300
Into Mr. Asdollah-Mirza's belly,

1234
00:45:48,800 --> 00:45:50,675
So now you don't know where Uncle Asdollah is?

1235
00:45:50,716 --> 00:45:51,716
He's nowhere to be found!

1236
00:45:52,300 --> 00:45:53,800
Honestly, my boy, why should I lie!

1237
00:45:54,050 --> 00:45:54,800
It's as if

1238
00:45:55,175 --> 00:45:58,091
He went up in smoke.

1239
00:46:00,550 --> 00:46:02,216
Or maybe out of fear of Mr. Dustali-Khan

1240
00:46:02,216 --> 00:46:03,925
He went and hid somewhere!

1241
00:46:04,300 --> 00:46:05,675
Now I suppose we'll also have a fight

1242
00:46:05,675 --> 00:46:07,550
Over finding Uncle Asdollah!

1243
00:46:09,300 --> 00:46:12,050
Your father sure knows how to stir things up, huh!

1244
00:46:13,800 --> 00:46:14,591
Last night,

1245
00:46:14,591 --> 00:46:15,466
At midnight…

1246
00:46:15,550 --> 00:46:16,925
This fellow townsman of ours…

1247
00:46:17,175 --> 00:46:20,216
He dragged Aspiran Ghias Abadi into the garden!

1248
00:46:21,216 --> 00:46:22,925
We heard from behind the trees.

1249
00:46:23,800 --> 00:46:25,175
He was telling him

1250
00:46:25,175 --> 00:46:27,716
That Mr. Asdollah-Mirza had killed Dustali-Khan.

1251
00:46:28,425 --> 00:46:30,675
By God's grace, we heard it from there!

1252
00:46:31,425 --> 00:46:33,550
We went after this Ghias Abadi!

1253
00:46:33,550 --> 00:46:36,175
And made him understand they're on bad terms!

1254
00:46:36,216 --> 00:46:38,425
That they want to stir up trouble for each other!

1255
00:46:39,716 --> 00:46:40,716
So if it weren't for you,

1256
00:46:40,800 --> 00:46:43,216
That Nayeb Teymoor-Khan would probably

1257
00:46:43,300 --> 00:46:44,341
Have shown up here again today!

1258
00:46:44,425 --> 00:46:45,716
♪ Traditional music ♪

1259
00:46:46,175 --> 00:46:47,050
Mash Ghasem!

1260
00:46:47,716 --> 00:46:49,175
Will you do something for me?

1261
00:46:50,091 --> 00:46:51,716
Can I ask you a favor?

1262
00:46:52,466 --> 00:46:54,050
I'm afraid to go to Dear Uncle’s house.

1263
00:46:54,216 --> 00:46:56,175
Could you tell Leili to come to the garden for a minute?

1264
00:46:57,800 --> 00:47:00,675
If I'm not wrong, you're sweet on Miss Leili!

1265
00:47:03,050 --> 00:47:04,466
Nothing wrong with that, my boy!

1266
00:47:04,675 --> 00:47:05,800
Go yourself!

1267
00:47:06,300 --> 00:47:07,925
Truth is, we're afraid of Sir!

1268
00:47:08,425 --> 00:47:09,591
After those two slaps last night

1269
00:47:09,591 --> 00:47:11,550
He landed on Mr. Dustali-Khan!

1270
00:47:12,091 --> 00:47:13,425
Go yourself!

1271
00:47:13,425 --> 00:47:15,091
Through the basement!

1272
00:47:17,716 --> 00:47:19,716
Miss Leili is in the women's quarters.

1273
00:47:20,425 --> 00:47:21,675
If Sir shows up,

1274
00:47:21,675 --> 00:47:23,425
Beat it through that same basement door!

1275
00:47:23,800 --> 00:47:24,550
Go on, my boy!

1276
00:47:24,841 --> 00:47:25,591
By the way, Mash Ghasem!

1277
00:47:26,800 --> 00:47:28,675
Don't let that sputtering Poori go tell Dear Uncle!

1278
00:47:28,675 --> 00:47:30,550
Don't worry, my boy!

1279
00:47:31,425 --> 00:47:34,175
Did you hear Mr. Poori was drafted?

1280
00:47:35,550 --> 00:47:40,341
♪ Traditional music ♪

